{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/5927","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:57:12.922850+00:00","comments":[],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### Describe the bug\n\nWhen using `fp_to_fp` with RTNE semantics to go from F16 to F8E5M2 on H100, Triton issues the following instruction:\n\n```\ncvt.rn.satfinite.e5m2x2.f16x2 ...\n```\n\nThis instruction does not preserve infinities due to the (mandatory) `.satfinite` modifier, but the IEEE 754 standard states that such a conversion, in RTNE mode, should map `inf` to `inf`.\n\nIt seems like this lowering path should only be used given `fastmath` option allowing not to preserve infinities---and otherwise a slower (but numerically correct) path should be chosen.\n\n### Environment details\n\nGPU: H100","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":0,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/5927/comments","created_at":"2025-02-14T12:59:40Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/5927/events","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/5927","id":2853662151,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"fc2929","default":true,"description":null,"id":125679820,"name":"bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMjU2Nzk4MjA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/labels/bug"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/5927/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOAWaHXs6qF23H","number":5927,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/5927/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tr